    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d710">

                <pb facs="0835" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg823"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114A Pacific War/221a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-10-23">October 23, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2416. Request Swiss Government to inform its Minister Tokyo that this Government
                    has reports of Japanese radio broadcasts to the effect <pb facs="0836" n="824"
                        xml:id="pg824"/> that the Japanese authorities intend to try before military
                    tribunals American prisoners of war for military operations and to impose upon
                    them severe penalties, including even the death penalty. Other reports state
                    that Japanese radio broadcasts are to the effect that such trials have already
                    taken place.</p>
                <p>Ask Swiss Minister urgently to report the facts regarding the foregoing. Also
                    request report, whether, in accordance with the Japanese Government’s
                    undertaking to apply the Geneva Prisoners of War Convention, Swiss
                    representatives have been permitted to visit the prisoners in question as
                    provided in Article 86 of the Convention.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
